node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Scheduler transcripts written by tools/scheduled/task.cmd. Machine-local
# operational noise - runs/<run-id>/run.json is the observability contract.
logs/
# Client raw data. `runs/<run-id>/snapshot.json` holds the real Google searches people
# typed to reach a client's site (707 distinct queries for `art`, 267 of them carrying a
# condition or injury term), their landing pages, click/impression counts, and the client's
# street addresses. `diagnostics/` holds SERP captures. This repo is public, so none of it
# is published from here on (operator decision, 2026-08-16). Untracked with
# `git rm -r --cached` at the same time - a .gitignore rule alone does nothing to files git
# already tracks. The files stay on disk and remain the system of record locally; a fresh
# clone simply has no run history. Commits already pushed are not affected by this.
projects/*/loops/*/runs/
projects/*/diagnostics/
# Derived SEO dashboard artifacts (tools/seo_timeseries.py, tools/gsc_daily.py).
# 100% rebuildable in under a second from runs/*/snapshot.json, which is the system
# of record - so committing a regenerated multi-hundred-KB blob every week buys
# nothing. Ignored by PATH, not by filename, so a new artifact cannot silently
# escape the rule (PLAN-SEO-TIMESERIES.md Q1, default = hold).
projects/*/loops/*/timeseries/
